From 665a8ce61bdea16bcfb07cc7b303ba7ee86dee2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 94xhn <87560781+94xhn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 07:19:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rr: fix TXT parser reading past declared RDLENGTH in
 rr_read_TXT()

rr_read_TXT() only checked the length-prefix byte of each TXT chunk
against the remaining receive-buffer size (*n), never against the
record's own declared RDLENGTH (len). Since len is a uint16_t and the
loop decrements it by (l + 1) on every iteration, a malformed TXT
answer whose embedded length byte exceeds the bytes actually remaining
in the record makes len underflow and wrap to a large value, letting
the parser keep walking past its own RDLENGTH boundary into unrelated
trailing packet bytes and allocate spurious TXT nodes from that data.

Add a bound check against the record's remaining declared length
before consuming each length-prefixed chunk, rejecting the record
immediately instead of wrapping.
---
 src/rr.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rr.c b/src/rr.c
index 2414a18..13b106d 100644
--- a/src/rr.c
+++ b/src/rr.c
@@ -183,6 +183,8 @@ rr_read_TXT(const uint8_t *ptr, size_t *n, const uint8_t *root, struct rr_entry
                 struct rr_data_txt *text;
 
                 memcpy(&l, ptr, sizeof(l));
+                if ((uint16_t)(l + 1) > len)
+                        return (NULL);
                 advance(1);
                 if (*n < l)
                         return (NULL);
